{
 "_about": "PHASE 8C.2 context-control regression set. KNOWN cases use the brief's own phrasing (and the implementation examples); HOLDOUT cases are unseen paraphrases written for evaluation only — no routing code, prompt or unit test contains them. Each case is a multi-step script in a fresh conversation; a step's expect is scored against that step, and step indexes refer to earlier steps of the same case. FRESH cases were written after the last change to routing code and were run once, unmodified, for the report.",
